--
-- Data for Name: ChangeLog; Type: TABLE DATA; Schema: public; Owner: postgres
--


- **Send and revoke team invites** — **Team** page, invite button
- **Finish setting up half-created users** (invited, no role assigned yet) —
  **Team → All** tab, open the user
- **Assign drivers to zones**, including adding yourself as a driver — **Team →**
  open a user **→ Driver** tab, zone picker
- **Load QuickBooks sales tax when building a quote** — **Quotes & Bookings → New
  Quote**, the **Tax** line in the totals panel

Invite failures on the **Team** page now say what actually went wrong ("this
email already exists", "badly formatted", "too many attempts") instead of
"Failed to invite user".

---

### 📄 Quotes

All on the **public quote page** — the link you send the client.

- **Clients can''t sign a quote that changed underneath them.** Edit a quote they
  have open and their page shows _"This quote has been updated"_ within ~10
  seconds. If they try to sign from the **Signed Contract** tab anyway, the
  server re-checks the terms at signing time and refuses. Previewing your own
  quote while signed in won''t trigger any of this.
- **The page works on a phone.** Clients open these on mobile constantly.
- **Clearer payment wording** on the **Pay Invoice** tab — "Due Now" / "Due on
  \<date\>" / "Final Due on \<date\>", plus a note that clients can **pay by ACH
  or check**, not just card.

---

### 🚚 Scheduling

- **Moving an accepted trip now asks first.** Dragging a work tracker on the
  **Dashboard** grid that a driver already accepted drops it back to Released and
  makes them re-accept — you now get a **"Move Accepted Trip?"** confirmation
  before that happens.
- Drivers only get notified for changes that affect them. In the **work tracker
  modal**: date, driver, address, time and pay changes un-accept and notify;
  notes-only changes just notify; minor edits stay quiet.
- **Distance tooltip** — **Dashboard → Options → Show Distance Tooltip**. Hover a
  bleacher cell to see the drive between its last and next location
  (`264.8 mi (426.1 km)`). Turning it on turns **Show Address Tooltip** off; only
  one can be active.

---

### 🔒 Security

- **Payment records are locked down.** The payment history table (payer names,
  emails, amounts, receipts) was reachable through the API. It isn''t anymore. No
  customer data is known to have been accessed.
- **Quote links are no longer guessable** — they used the sequential invoice
  number, so someone could walk the list and read other customers'' quotes.

⚠️ **Old quote links stop working.** No client links have been sent yet, so this
affects nobody in practice — but re-copy any quote URL you saved in a note or
draft email.

---

### 🐛 Fixes

- **Your own driver-zone assignment no longer vanishes on save** — **Team →** your
  user **→ Driver** tab. It said "User updated successfully" and silently threw
  the zone away.
- **Damage reports can''t be marked resolved without a repair.** In the damage
  report on **Quality Assurance → Damage Reports**, the resolved toggle is gone,
  replaced by **Create Maintenance to Resolve** — so a closed report always points
  at real work.
- **One Linxup device can now be tracked on multiple bleachers** — **Assets →
  Bleachers →** the **Linxup Device** field.
- **Dashboard zone filtering fixed** — the zone selector beside **Options**.

---

You''re reading this on the new **What''s New** page (**Product** menu in the top
bar, or **Documentation** in the sidebar). You''ll see a **New** badge on
**Product** whenever there''s something here you haven''t read.
'),
	('087cdb21-c7ca-4396-bf22-73e0cc106a23', '1.1.0', '2026-08-13 15:32:44.981316+00', '### ✍️ Clients can sign again after you edit a booked quote

**The big one.** If you edited a quote the client had already signed, their
**Signed Contract** tab on the **public quote page** kept showing "already
signed" — so they could never sign the revised terms, and the system couldn''t
record a new signature either. You were stuck chasing it outside the app.

Editing contract terms now automatically retires the old signature and puts the
signing form back in front of the client.

- **Counts as a contract change:** price and line items, event dates, venue
  address, payment schedule, taxes, terms & conditions, sales office.
- **Doesn''t:** client notes and PO number — edit those freely without making
  anyone re-sign.

The original signature is never deleted. It''s a legal record, so the signature
and its PDF stay on file and are only marked as superseded.

---

### 💳 Payments

- **A real confirmation screen.** Paying on the **Pay Invoice** tab now lands the
  client on a dedicated success page with a **Back to Quote** button, instead of
  a banner buried on the tab they just left. Before this release it was a **404**
  — the redirect still used the old invoice-number link that moved in 1.0.0,
  which reads like the payment failed.
- **Payment History records payments again.** Stripe''s webhook wasn''t pointed at
  the app, so completed payments never wrote a row. Payments now appear with
  their receipt link in the **Payment History** section — **Quotes & Bookings →**
  open a quote **→ Billing** tab for you, and the client''s **Pay Invoice** tab
  for them.
- **Payment notification emails are firing.** The payment-made templates for both
  the client and the account manager were inactive in **Email Automation**
  settings, so nothing sent after a successful payment. Both are configured and
  live now.

The money always reached Stripe throughout — what broke was the client''s
confirmation and our record of it. **Check any payment taken before this release
against Stripe**, since it may be missing from Payment History.

---

### 🔎 Smaller

- The top bar now shows which version you''re on — **App Version 1.1.0**, the same
  menu as **What''s New**. Worth quoting when you report a problem.
- The **Make Checks Payable To** address on the **Pay Invoice** tab no longer
  repeats the city and state.
'),
	('e96af3aa-2303-47e1-80d8-e56ec115ab48', '1.1.1', '2026-08-13 18:34:22.331506+00', '### 📄 Shorter company address on the quote you send clients

On the **public quote page** — the link clients open — the company address
is now a single line of **street, city, state and ZIP**. instead of duplicate city and state. It shows up in three spots: the
letterhead at the top, the **Make checks payable to:** box beside the
**Totals** panel, and the last tab. All three used to wrap onto a second line carrying the duplicate city
and state.
'),
	('b2f11f2f-081f-4655-a2b7-4b8c14cf43ea', '1.1.2', '2026-08-14 16:40:45.737854+00', '### 📍 Same cleanup, now on the event address

1.1.1 tidied the **company** address. This does the **venue** address — the
one that says where the bleachers actually go. It''s now a single line of
**street and ZIP** in all three places it shows up:

- **Public quote page** — the **Location / Venue** block in the header
- **The quote PDF** you email or download — the **Event Venue** block
- **Quotes & Bookings →** open a quote **→ Contract** tab — the **Venue**
  section

As before, nothing is lost: the street line already includes the city and
state, so the old second line was just repeating them.
'),
	('b205245d-95e8-4500-a736-f2bf7418abcc', '1.2.0', '2026-08-14 21:10:01.900549+00', '### 💰 Driver pay by distance, not one flat rate

**Team →** open a driver **→ Driver** tab **→ Manager Setup**. The old **Pay
Rate** box is gone. In its place is a line running from **0** to **∞**, showing
what the driver earns across the whole trip length:

```
0MI ———— $3.00/MI ———— 100MI ———— $2.50/MI ———— 200MI ———— $2.25/MI ———— ∞MI
```

[Watch it in action](https://www.loom.com/share/ef3d4570b73f469990e31145ca3e7d77)

- **Click the line** to add a cutoff. It asks for the value, in that driver''s unit.
- **Click a rate** to change it.
- **Click a cutoff** to move it, or remove it — removing merges the two ranges
  either side.

A driver with no ranges is one unbroken line showing a single rate, exactly like
the old box. Nothing to set up unless you want tiers.

**Currency**, **Per Unit** and **Tax** stay where they were, above the line.
Cutoffs are in whatever **Per Unit** says — KM, MI or HR — so switching the unit
switches what the numbers mean.

**Who can edit:** admins, and account managers who share a zone with the driver
— the same rule that already governs the rest of that driver''s details.

---

### 🧮 The pay calculator uses those ranges, and shows its work

**Work Trackers →** open a trip **→** the **calculator icon** beside the **Pay**
box. It now picks the rate for the distance actually travelled instead of always
using the base rate. **Hover it** before clicking and it spells out the sum:

![The pay calculator tooltip showing the distance, rate and total](/changelog/1.2.0-calculate-pay-screenshot.png)

One rate covers the whole trip — the range the trip lands in. A 150-mile trip in
a **100–200 @ $2.50** range is 150 × $2.50, not part-priced at each tier below
it.

Drivers with no ranges calculate exactly as they always did, at their base rate —
as does a trip that falls outside every range you''ve set.
'),
	('96cc80e6-04ef-45b6-b236-158a090f60f5', '1.2.1', '2026-08-18 18:18:03.342681+00', '### 🔄 More reliable startup when you have several tabs open

When you open the app in more than one Chrome tab — including after your browser
restores tabs — the local data service now starts reliably instead of leaving the
app on its loading screen.

This change was prompted by a real incident where the app got stuck on an infinite
loading screen and required switching to a different browser and clearing cached
data to recover. To prevent this from happening again, the underlying local data
service has been updated to use a more broadly compatible storage approach. This
comes with a modest tradeoff in raw startup speed, but the result is a much more
predictable and stable experience — especially after browser updates or when
multiple tabs are involved.
'),
	('bc831c3d-cd16-4cd3-820f-5311b14da0dd', '1.2.2', '2026-08-18 19:09:11.604828+00', '### 🖱️ Work trackers are easier to move on the Dashboard

On the **Dashboard schedule grid**, a small work tracker displayed over an event
can now be picked up and moved reliably. The cursor no longer flickers between
the trip and the event, and the event no longer interrupts the drag.

This makes it easier for account managers to reschedule driver work without
opening each work tracker first.

| Before                                                                         | After                                                                           |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| [Watch the issue](https://www.loom.com/share/b3f17ddb2e3e47eca3e02e8337abaa6f) | [Watch it working](https://www.loom.com/share/8e03221a71a84d839857739006a8a338) |
'),
	('262a4813-5ed8-4466-8617-7ced14191ce2', '1.3.0', '2026-08-20 16:02:15.031458+00', '### 💵 See every part of a driver''s pay on the trip

**Work Trackers →** open a trip **→ Line Items** tab. You can now itemize hauling,
deadhead, setup, teardown, maintenance, per diem and custom work with a quantity,
rate, description and total.

- **Hauling and deadhead calculate automatically** from the route and selected
  driver''s rates.
- Checking **Setup Required** or **Teardown Required** on the **Details** tab adds
  the matching line; unchecking it removes that line.
- Set each driver''s deadhead rate under **Team →** open the driver **→ Driver** tab
  **→ Manager Setup → Deadhead Rate**.

---

### 🚚 Fix trips without stopping the driver''s progress

Account managers can now edit or move trips that are in progress, completed or
cancelled. Open the **work tracker modal** to correct the details, or drag the trip
on the **Dashboard schedule grid**. An in-progress trip keeps its current status,
and the assigned driver is notified when a change affects them.
'),
	('f43fe06f-a427-4a15-ac36-ed284dc06f27', '1.4.0', '2026-08-20 19:36:12.183991+00', '### 📸 Damage report photos: smaller uploads, iPhone photos just work

**Damage Reports page →** create or edit a report. Photos are now resized and
compressed before upload, and iPhone HEIC photos are converted automatically —
no more "invalid file type" errors when a driver''s photo comes straight off
their phone.

- Up to **30 photos** per report.
- A damage severity, a note, and at least one photo are now required before
  you can save a report.

---

### 🕓 Reports no longer show up before their photos are ready

**Damage Reports page.** A report created over a weak signal used to appear
in the list right away, even while its photos were still uploading in the
background — looking incomplete or broken. New reports now stay hidden until
every photo is confirmed uploaded.

- Developers can click **Hiding Uploading Photos** (top-right) to reveal
  reports that are still mid-upload for troubleshooting.
'),
	('0b1001f6-0660-4914-b5b9-bd2f31d6a7a7', '1.5.0', '2026-08-21 16:36:31.753018+00', '### 💵 Setup and teardown pay now follows each driver

**Team →** open a driver **→ Driver tab → Manager Setup.** Admins can now set
flat **Setup Pay** and **Teardown Pay** amounts alongside the driver''s deadhead
rate.

**Work Trackers →** open a trip. When **Setup Required** or **Teardown Required**
is selected, the matching **Line Items** row now uses that driver''s saved rate.
The calculator beside **Driver Pay** sets the payment to the full line-items total,
including hauling, deadhead, setup, teardown and any custom work.
'),
	('109e21ec-66eb-463e-babd-b7f5e296b3cc', '1.6.0', '2026-08-27 15:22:46.858905+00', '### 🇫🇷 Quotes can now go out in French

**Companies & Contacts →** open a contact **→ Edit → Quote Language.** Set a
contact to French and everything they receive arrives in French: the quote page,
the contract they sign, the payment screen and the PDF. The same dropdown sits on
the new-contact form, including the one inside the quote builder.

Dates and amounts follow Canadian French convention — `15 janv. 2026` and
`1 234,56 $`. English quotes are untouched.

Terms & Conditions are not translated for you: write a French T&C document and
select it on the quote as usual.

Clients can also fix the language themselves from the globe icon at the top of
their quote — useful when a contact was set up wrong. That switch shows up in
**Quote → Log → Customer Activity**, so you know to correct the contact record.

### 🚚 Drivers can report which bleacher they actually took

When the assigned bleacher is buried at the back of the yard, drivers take an
equivalent one from the front. They can now say so when submitting an inspection,
with a reason — blocked, damaged, hard to get to, or not on site.

**You get a push notification** naming the trip, the bleacher taken and why.
Inspections and damage reports are filed against the bleacher that actually went
out, not the one on paper.

The Bill of Lading and bleacher availability still show the bleacher you
assigned. Reconciling the two stays your call — the notification is the prompt.

### 📇 Point of contact fills itself in on work trackers

**Work Trackers →** open a trip **→ Details.** Pickup and Dropoff POC are now
real contact records instead of typed-in text, so the phone number travels with
the name. The locate button beside each pulls the POC from the booked event or
the neighbouring trip — the same way the address locate button already works.

If the neighbouring trip only has a typed-in name with no contact behind it, the
button tells you to create the contact first rather than copying a name with no
number attached.

### ⚡ Create a work tracker straight from the dashboard

**Dashboard →** ⌘+click an empty cell (Ctrl+click on Windows) to open a new work
tracker for that bleacher and date, skipping the popup. The truck button in the
cell popup still works. Both run the same permission checks, so you can still
only create trackers on bleachers that are yours.

### 🧭 Fixes

**Work Trackers →** the driver list now follows zones. You see the drivers who
share a zone with you, matching how the rest of the app already works. Admins and
the **See All Drivers** toggle still show everyone.

**Companies & Contacts →** contact and company forms now catch bad email
addresses and phone numbers, flagging a field only once you''ve left it. Save
stays disabled until the required fields are filled.
'),
	('05197d73-4870-4689-a916-767e97c24152', '1.7.0', '2026-08-31 13:47:36.159504+00', '### 🔀 See at a glance which events are in GoodShuffle

**Quotes & Bookings →** every event that is linked to GoodShuffle now carries the
GoodShuffle logo beside its name in the table. Hover it and it tells you what it
means.

**Quotes & Bookings → Filters → In GoodShuffle.** A new dropdown with three
choices: **Any** leaves the list alone, **Yes** shows only linked events, and
**No** shows only the ones still waiting to be linked — useful for finding what
has slipped through.

An event with an empty GoodShuffle field counts as **not** linked, so the "No"
list is the real list of work left to do.
'),
	('9ec4f54b-dba7-40f9-b017-adff62dd5a3e', '1.8.0', '2026-08-31 18:10:37.966506+00', '### 📊 Ask your drivers how it''s going, and see the answers

**Driver Satisfaction** is a new page, beside the two scorecards in the sidebar.

Drivers are asked one question in the mobile app — how satisfied they are
overall, out of ten — and anyone scoring 6 or below is asked why in their own
words. Nobody is asked on a schedule: a driver is asked after their first
completed trip, then again once enough days have passed since they last answered.
Someone who has been away for months comes back to **one** question, not a queue
of them.

The page shows the **average score**, how many drivers **need a follow-up**, how
many are **promoters**, and how many drivers you have **heard from** at all.
Below that, a trend over time and the full list of responses. Change the period
or filter by score and everything moves together.

Account managers and viewers can read all of it.

### 🎫 Drivers can report problems without leaving the app

A driver who hits a problem can now file a ticket straight from the mobile app.
It lands in **Roadmap → Backlog** like any other, and the card says who sent it,
so you know whether you are reading a manager''s request or a driver''s.

They can tidy up their own ticket for a short while after sending it. They see
nothing else on the roadmap.

### ⚡ The roadmap saves as you go

**Roadmap →** clicking **+ New Feature**, **+ New Task** or **+ Submit Ticket**
now creates the record straight away and opens it for editing. No more filling in
a blank form and losing it if something goes wrong.

Edits save themselves as you type, with an indicator showing when the last one
landed. If a save fails — a dropped connection, usually — it tells you instead of
pretending. Deleting is a soft delete, so a record removed by mistake is
recoverable.

### 📄 Driver documents: look before you download

**Team →** open a driver **→ Driver tab.** Licences, insurance and medical cards
can be previewed in place rather than downloaded first, and each now takes an
**expiry date** — so an out-of-date document can actually be spotted.
'),
	('955bc659-325c-4698-94ef-12c8e50fb28c', '1.8.1', '2026-09-02 20:38:08.936779+00', '### 🍁 Canadian quotes now work out their own tax

**Quotes & Bookings →** create or edit a quote **→ Totals.** A quote for an event
in Canada now fills in the right tax on its own — 13% in Ontario, 14.975% in
Quebec, 5% in Alberta, and so on for every province and territory. Until now the
tax line stayed empty for Canadian addresses and somebody had to know the rate
and type it in.

The rate follows the **event address**, not the sales office, which is how
Canadian tax actually works: what you charge depends on where the bleachers end
up. Quebec''s rate runs to three decimal places, and the tax line shows all of
them rather than rounding.

### 🚧 A quote can''t straddle the border

If the **Sales Office** and the **event address** are in different countries — a
Canadian office with an American event address, or the other way round — the
quote now says so in red rather than quietly leaving the tax blank. Pick an
office in the same country as the event, or enter the tax yourself.

### ✉️ A warning before a quote can''t be sent

**Quotes & Bookings →** create or edit a quote **→ Account Manager.** Picking
someone whose email is not a **@bleacherrentals.com** address now shows a warning
under the dropdown.

Quotes go out from the account manager''s own address, so a personal one can''t
send at all. Better to find that out while filling in the quote than at the
moment you press send.
'),
	('fd474657-a6f5-44c3-9f7e-0c40899c741f', '1.9.0', '2026-09-04 14:39:49.657156+00', '### 💵 Record a payment that never went through Stripe

**Quotes & Bookings →** open a quote **→ Billing tab → + Record Payment.** The
button used to be greyed out. Now it opens a dialog for a check, an ACH transfer
or a card run by hand on a terminal, with the date, the payer, a reference number
and a note.

A recorded payment can never be edited or deleted. A mistake — a bounced check, a
refund, a wrong amount — is corrected by recording the same amount as a
**negative**, so both entries stay on the record and the history reads like a
ledger. Recording a refund here does not send money back through Stripe; that is
still done in Stripe.

Administrators and lead account managers can record a payment on any quote. Other
account managers can do it on the quotes they created. Viewers cannot, but they
can still read everything.

### 🔍 The payment history now says what actually happened

**Billing tab.** Amounts come from the money that actually arrived rather than
from a paid/unpaid flag, so an installment that has received part of what it is
owed now shows as **partial** instead of jumping straight to paid. Clicking any
payment opens the full record — every installment it was applied to, the
reference, the notes and who entered it.

The client''s own **Pay** tab is worked out the same way, so the balance they see
and the balance you see cannot disagree.

### ✍️ Paying an installment no longer invalidates the signature

A client who paid an installment was immediately asked to re-sign a contract they
had already signed, and was shown a "this quote has been updated" notice for a
payment they had just made themselves. Nothing about the agreement had changed —
only money had arrived. Both are fixed.

While we were in there, the client''s Pay tab now says an amount is **"Due"**
rather than **"Overdue"**, which is what it usually is.

### 📊 Subtotal and tax, side by side on the list

**Quotes & Bookings.** The single **Amount** column is now **Subtotal** and
**Tax**, each with its own total in the column header. Canadian and American
quotes are totalled separately rather than added together, and every figure is
shown in the currency the quote is actually priced in.

Long event names now shorten cleanly with the full name on hover, instead of
being chopped off mid-word.

### 🏢 Filter by sales office

**Quotes & Bookings → Filters.** A new **Sales Office** dropdown narrows the list
to one office. "All Sales Offices" clears it in one click.

Office names in the quote form now carry the currency they actually sell in —
`Ontario Office (CAD)`. An office whose address is missing a province used to be
offered as USD while the quote it produced was priced and charged in CAD.

### 📒 Mark a quote as invoiced in QuickBooks

**Billing tab → QuickBooks.** A **QuickBooks Invoice** checkbox records by hand
that an event has been invoiced. It is bookkeeping only — nothing is pushed to
QuickBooks — and the change is logged, so you can see who ticked it and when.

Administrators and account managers can set it on any quote, including ones they
did not create — bookkeeping is not the quote owner''s job. Viewers can see it but
not change it.

### 📝 Two smaller things on a new quote

**+ Create Quote** now starts with the standard delivery-window and interest
disclaimer already in **Client-Facing Notes**, so nobody has to remember to paste
it. A draft you had already started is left alone.

A blank quote can now be saved as a draft. Save no longer refuses because the
event name or dates are empty — it files it as an untitled draft for you to
finish later. Sending a quote still requires everything.

### ✉️ E-transfer instructions on the quote

The "make checks payable to" box on the quote a client sees now also gives the
e-transfer address, in English and in French.

### 🧹 Fixes

- **Event chat:** opening the chat on an event you own occasionally failed
  outright, and quietly put you back in a chat you had deliberately left. An
  owner who leaves now stays out, and rejoins with the **Join** button like
  anyone else.
- **Sidebar:** long section names no longer push the sidebar wide or spill past
  its edge.
'),
	('40d6984d-2266-4098-b3ce-e60d3b781b03', '1.10.0', '2026-09-04 20:49:55.814725+00', '### 🇨🇦 Driver tax now supports Quebec''s rate

**Manage Team → a driver → Driver section.** The tax rate field used to only
take whole percent, so Quebec''s 14.975% got typed in and quietly stored as 14.
Every payout worked out from that driver''s tax was short. The field now takes
decimals — type `14.975` and it stays `14.975`.

### 🔢 Work tracker quantities no longer round to whole units

**Work Trackers → a driver''s week → Line Items tab.** A half day of setup or
2.5 hours of maintenance used to have to be rounded to a whole number before it
could be entered, so the pay for that line was off by up to half a unit''s
worth. The quantity field now takes one decimal place, so `2.5` is `2.5`.

### 💵 Filter the weekly driver list by currency

**Work Trackers → a week.** A new **Currency** dropdown next to "See All
Drivers" narrows the list to CAD or USD drivers only. "All Currencies" clears
it.

### 🔗 Quotes & Bookings remembers your filters when you come back

**Quotes & Bookings.** Opening a quote and hitting the browser''s back button
used to dump you back onto an empty, unfiltered list. Filters, the search box,
and Show Deleted now round-trip through the page''s URL, so back restores the
list exactly as you left it — and the link itself can be copied or bookmarked
with those filters baked in.
'),
	('6bf7d610-c9b1-45f2-b6ae-4837ffa69c80', '1.11.0', '2026-09-09 14:57:37.14216+00', '### 🕘 Pickup and dropoff time: Exact, Flexible, or Any Time

**Work Trackers → open a tracker → Pickup/Dropoff Time.** Pickup and dropoff
time used to be a free-text box, so it sorted and displayed however it was
typed. It''s now a picker with three options: **Exact** (one time), **Flexible**
(a from/to window), or **Any Time** — every tracker that never had a time set
now shows "Any Time" instead of blank. Trips within the same day now sort by
their actual pickup time on the weekly trip list, the driver PDF, and the
admin''s all-work-trackers table.

![Pickup Time field showing Exact, Flexible, and Any Time options, with Flexible selected and a from/to range of 8:00 AM to 9:00 AM](/changelog/1.11.0-pickup-time.png)

### 🚚 Work tracker type is now a color-coded picker

**Work Trackers → open a tracker.** Type used to be a free-text field. It''s
now a dropdown with three fixed options — **Trip**, **Repair/Maintenance**, and
**Site Visit/Cleaning/Other** — each with its own color and icon. Only Trip
shows separate Pickup and Dropoff sections and the route map; the other two
types collapse to one generic set of fields (still Setup/Teardown Required and
all), and the Bill of Lading PDF follows the same layout.

![The Type dropdown open, showing Trip, Repair / Maintenance, and Site Visit / Cleaning / Other, each with its own icon](/changelog/1.11.0-worktracker-types.png)

**Configuration → Work Tracker Types** (admin only) now only edits which
QuickBooks account each of the 3 types posts to. The old page that let anyone
add, rename, or delete types is gone.

Until the next driver mobile app release, all work trackers will still appear to
drivers as if they are Trips, even when they are a different type in the admin
app.

### 🕐 Drive Time and Mileage on the weekly trip list

**Work Trackers → a driver''s week.** Two new columns, on the page and in the
downloaded PDF, showing each trip''s drive time (e.g. "2.4 hrs") and distance
(e.g. "21.4 mi (34.4 km)"), with a total on the SubTotal row.

![The driver PDF showing new Time and Drive Time columns, with Drive Time and Milage highlighted](/changelog/1.11.0-worktracker-milage.png)
'),
	('78a88779-5fdb-4995-995c-be544325ba8c', '1.12.0', '2026-09-10 23:15:28.251251+00', '### 🔧 Annual bleacher inspections, tracked and chased automatically

**Sidebar → Annual Inspections** (admins and viewers; a new role, below, owns
this page). Every bleacher now has an inspection record — a due date, the
certificate, and a note — instead of living in someone''s memory or a
spreadsheet. A bleacher is flagged **yellow 30 days before it''s due, red at 7
days, and red once it''s overdue**, and the list can be filtered down to just
what needs attention.

Recording an inspection is unchanged for account managers — still done from
the bleacher''s own edit sheet — but the queue page itself belongs to the new
Maintainer role.

### 👷 A new team role: Maintainer

**Manage Team → + New User.** Maintainer is a role built for one job: owning
the Annual Inspections queue. A maintainer sees Annual Inspections and nothing
else, and they''re the only one who gets chased about it — the notification
badge and row highlighting only ever appear for a maintainer, so it reads as a
real to-do list instead of noise everyone learns to ignore.

### ✅ A driver can mark damage already fixed — close it without a maintenance event

**Damage Reports → open a report.** When a driver has already fixed something
themselves, the report now shows **"Fixed by [Driver] on [date]"**, and a
**Mark as Resolved** button sits next to Create Maintenance to Resolve — no
need to invent a maintenance event for a repair that never has to happen.

### 🔁 Duplicate damage reports become one report with a confirmation count

**Damage Reports → open a report.** Drivers who see damage someone already
reported now confirm the existing report instead of filing a second one about
the same thing. That report shows **"Confirmed by N drivers"** with who and
when, so a quiet damage list reads as "handled," not as "nobody''s reporting
anymore."

### 🩹 A maintainer-only account no longer shows as an incomplete setup

**Manage Team.** The "Incomplete User Setup" check didn''t know about the new
Maintainer role, so a maintainer account looked broken and the banner implied
they couldn''t sign in. Fixed.

### 💰 Finance now gets a copy of account manager quote and payment emails

Every "quote signed" and "payment made" email that goes to an account manager
now also goes to finance@bleacherrentals.com — no more waiting to hear
secondhand.
');


