	('a9128cfd-514b-4a45-a2a7-1f0374812b5d', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', '99776dbb-8ab2-4d98-bc73-d808d106bc5e', 'PO #', '<p>jkust a spot to track if a client gives a PO number we can call and reference. PO is in THEIR system</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-09 13:52:24.841+00', '2026-06-12 13:52:26.911037+00', NULL),
	('13becba6-e3e8-4cef-8699-9cb99aae7e7a', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', '99776dbb-8ab2-4d98-bc73-d808d106bc5e', 'Fix Tax Problem', '<p>The schedule amount can be different from the subtotal when overriding tax.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-18 13:37:13.098+00', '2026-06-18 15:05:16.029257+00', NULL),
	('55fc8c18-f417-4d07-abae-ad861109a4e9', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', '99776dbb-8ab2-4d98-bc73-d808d106bc5e', 'Junior Account Manager Can''t Edit Quotes that are assigned to them.', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-18 21:43:07.489+00', '2026-06-22 16:10:52.05349+00', NULL),
	('f747fbdb-8dcd-4d6a-a61d-e6587ad29a30', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', NULL, 'Subtotal Order', '<p>Just need to delete one thing on the customer page.</p><p></p><p>Subtotal = 10000</p><p>discount = -1000</p><p>subtotal after discount = 9000</p><p>tax 13% = 199</p><p>Total</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-09 13:50:16.425+00', '2026-06-15 13:06:20.54553+00', NULL),
	('26db683b-e5f0-405a-add6-300db6f5c37d', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', NULL, 'DUE JUNE 16 - upload files - send quotes', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-09 13:34:26.196+00', '2026-06-15 16:55:58.319653+00', NULL),
	('b3cf91f7-cd60-4964-abf0-174bffc66dcd', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', '03e1a9ca-f418-4f24-8616-7e3e867ae63e', 'Damage Reports should show drivers name as Created by', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-09 14:00:27.405+00', '2026-06-17 22:29:58.481894+00', NULL),
	('3c07bc08-cb01-4151-bd4c-c95903619c07', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', '99776dbb-8ab2-4d98-bc73-d808d106bc5e', 'Process Payments with stripe - Send Quotes', '<p>Max got this really far but Josh needs to wire up the webhook stuff<br><br></p><p>We can receive payments on production but we should probably handle via webhook to mark things as paid in the db and be able to track payments over time and to get a receipt emailed to the user.<br><br>Maybe make sure we get the currency conversion stuff working.</p><p></p><p>okay should be working I already setup the webhook for production and then we can test with 50 cents or something once we deploy</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-09 13:32:57.913+00', '2026-06-18 00:37:54.601201+00', NULL),
	('b2fe5662-c204-4d64-81e6-07b3a0a5db91', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Selected Bleachers Should Always be Shown', '<p>Josh: "Make sure that the zone selector uses the same filter function that all the other filters go through. Make sure that no matter what in any case all selected bleachers for this event show. useCurrentEventStore is the in memory selected event after clicking an event span in the dashboard"<br>Mike: "When clicking an event, only the filtered events show, not all the bleachers in the event."<br></p><p>All bleachers reserved for events do not show up when you click on the evernt, the zone sorting overrides the event sorting, it should be opposite. we want to see all the bleacher booked regardless of zones selectex</p>', 'completed', 0, true, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', '2026-06-23 10:37:24.884+00', '2026-07-29 22:20:48.057147+00', NULL),
	('18fe94d4-60ae-4701-8522-a576bb93636f', '499b152d-7cde-4d20-8ea6-a7091de4e6d2', NULL, 'Driver Select different Bleacher number broken?', '<p>link the addresses</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-08 20:36:56.778+00', NULL, '2026-07-29 17:54:49.739+00'),
	('19c334d8-21a1-4264-b3cd-a4c613ce56d2', 'a3dad991-87b2-4219-9ea4-f2ab1fbcdd6e', '90e4e2a3-a387-4321-9b26-29b46175fdc1', 'Save empty quote as draft', '<p>• ⁃ Should be able to save quote as draft with almost no info but can only send it with the required fields.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-09-10 12:42:33.8+00', '2026-09-10 12:42:47.689706+00', NULL),
	('ba310757-72f8-429e-b6db-3d0f57bc16b3', '71d6e0b4-ffaa-42c5-9e58-5928044b24e3', NULL, 'Powersync 1000 Parameter Query limit error', '<p>we''re having an issue with driver app again i had to increase the limit but we should look into this.</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-09-10 12:34:10.382+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b84c991a-e77a-41ce-a1f1-440d522f502f', '71d6e0b4-ffaa-42c5-9e58-5928044b24e3', '90e4e2a3-a387-4321-9b26-29b46175fdc1', 'DO THIS LAST - Bleacher Type Description', '<p>Add an over writable description for each line item in the quote.</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-09-10 12:37:27.184+00', NULL, NULL),
	('6ad4b31e-7b4b-48dc-a70f-1eb4c7aa98c2', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', NULL, 'Damage Reports Suggestions', '<p>a message from gereth about the app. &nbsp;</p><p>Good morning, and happy Sunday!<br><br>I’d like to share some feedback on the app that I think will help streamline tracking repairs for the bleachers, especially when moving from driver to driver.<br>When we submit a pre-trip inspection that includes new damage or issues, the report currently moves to the post-trip section or stays with the bleacher when it’s assigned to the next driver. Could we set it up so the previous pre-trip/post-trip inspection is automatically carried over (pre-toggled)?<br><br>This would allow the next driver to:<br>-See what damage was previously reported<br>-Inspect whether the damage is still present<br>-Confirm if repairs were made or are still needed<br>- Update the status if damage has worsened or been fixed<br><br>For example, recently we had a light damaged at an event.. lucky they bleacher was staying at the same place for next event. We were able to report the damage and then next driver accepted the job and saw the reported damaged light in the app.<br>Being able to pick up that light before pre-trip, then mark it as fixed once repaired, would make it smoother..<br><br>Conversely, if a new pre-trip shows damaged railings, the driver could inspect them, assess whether the damage worsened, and note if any on-the-spot repairs are possible.<br><br>And it''ll save times when you bring bleachers back to a yard after being inspected at pick up from event. Unless something on the trip back. But everything pre toggle be easy to add anything additional<br><br>This change would greatly improve communication between drivers and make the repair process smoother.<br></p><p><br><br></p><p>Mike T</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-07 16:23:50.314+00', NULL, NULL),
	('dbd8beae-2ec6-4e52-ad78-10193ff03026', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', NULL, 'Move sales office to configuration drop down', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-15 16:59:42.936+00', '2026-06-16 14:12:26.434452+00', NULL),
	('327086f9-32c9-42bd-b8ea-4dcc0ca63bcf', NULL, NULL, 'Adjusting dates when work tracker pushes to QBO', '<p>I know it''s been discussed before in person but when work trackers are pushed to QBO the invoice date should be the start of the week, currently it grabs the last day in the week. And the due date I''m wondering if it would work to change it to the day the work tracker is sent to QBO. Right now I think it''s a week after the invoice date.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '788a4690-2a6f-4ad7-9365-3669d230aee0', '2026-06-12 18:07:58.921+00', NULL, NULL),
	('9ec183be-b069-49b3-b707-ddbe77afaf0a', 'd3056243-c26f-4f7c-ba49-92b608ac8a61', NULL, 'maybe mark events that have passed as Lost if they are quoted.', '<p>this could be an alert to the AMs saying "Wanna mark this event as lost?"</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-16 13:08:08.223+00', NULL, NULL),
	('a98ed355-071a-4299-b220-a3a1a5ac1b88', 'c4d83a6e-28fb-4ac3-9146-4892895595a4', NULL, 'ScoreCard Click to Show Quotes and Bookings', '<p>Should be able to click on a graph in the scorecard and open the quotes and bookings page with these filter options to see where the number came from in the score card.</p><p></p><p>Should also improve the filtering in general on the Quotes and Bookings page</p><p></p><p></p><p>Here, just try to actually use the exact same code that pulls and filters the events in the quotes and bookings page to get the data on the actual dashboard as well, or I should say on the actual scorecard.</p><p>I think we should have a standardized company time zone. We should cast everything to the Eastern Standard or America/Toronto time zone so that everybody from all around the world will see the same numbers. We''ll just put a note on the UI saying that everything is being cast to Eastern time zone or America/Toronto, which is where the company headquarters is, so that''s why we chose that one. The revenue does not seem to line up yet, so that doesn''t make sense, but at least we''re at a point where we can figure it out.</p><p>Coming up with the margin, we will need the driver pay, so we''ll need to create a driver''s table too. I say we either make a new page in the quotes and bookings page to look at all the work trackers, or we just add some filtering options to the work trackers page and show all the work trackers in a different view. We can clearly prove all the data that we''re getting using the same code. The only thing is, whenever I use quad to actually do this for me, I still don''t fully get the code that he''s writing, so I got to go through that and maybe make sense of it myself before pushing it. Some of it seems to work, some of it doesn''t seem to work.</p>', 'completed', 0, true, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-04-16 19:52:10.75+00', '2026-06-16 13:47:18.407311+00', NULL),
	('a4d502a7-4356-4627-bb44-3552e6bc0679', NULL, NULL, 'Click on Maintenance Event in Dashboard', '<p>When you click on the text of the event span in the dashbaord a click event is not registered. Please fix like you did with the regular event spans a while ago.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-05-04 16:43:59.385+00', NULL, '2026-06-16 13:52:41.992+00'),
