	('3311828c-b11d-45ed-b8b8-29718c12cd50', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Quote screen is mobile responsive', '<p>- Make sure the quote screen is mobile responsive</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:10:47.91+00', NULL, NULL),
	('559ca339-d8f4-4430-86fb-a2bd9a1ba66f', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Driver App - Make sure Photos work with driver profile', '<p>Make sure the offline photo submission also works with the driver profile. like medical card insurance and license photos. <br>ALSO make a RLS policy where no one can update or delete photos from this storage bucket. Include JPG conversion as well</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-22 13:11:46.126+00', '2026-07-23 13:42:05.163508+00', NULL),
	('1cf6c98b-1210-4dfd-bce4-0da6a2cc34f7', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Driver App - Suggest or Force Updates', '<p>We need to verify the version number with the server so if a driver is on an out-dated version of the mobile app we can restrict access until they update their application.</p><p></p><p>When a driver opens the app, compare their installed version to a server policy and:</p><ol><li><p>Soft recommend — “new version available” (OK / Update)</p></li><li><p>Countdown — warn with 3 / 2 / 1 days left</p></li><li><p>Hard block — must Update or Exit</p></li><li><p>Report each driver’s current app version for ops visibility</p></li></ol><p>Tables<br><code>app_version_policy</code> — always exactly 3 rows (one per environment). We don’t insert new rows per release; we update fields in the existing row.<br>Column/Purpose<br><code>environment can have development</code> / <code>staging</code> / <code>production</code> — so policies don’t cross environments<br><code>recommended_version</code>Soft target — below this → optional update prompt<br><code>required_version</code>Hard floor — below this → app blocked immediately<br><code>soft_deadline</code>Shared calendar date — after it, anyone still below recommended is force-blocked<br><code>ios_store_url</code> / <code>android_store_url</code>Store links for the Update button<br><code>message</code>Optional modal copy<br><br><br><br><code>Drivers</code> — new columns:</p><ul><li><p><code>app_version</code>— current installed version</p></li><li><p><code>app_platform</code>—<code>ios</code>/<code>android</code></p></li><li><p><code>app_version_reported_at</code>— last report time</p></li></ul><p><br><br>How it works</p><ol><li><p>Driver opens the app → app reads its version</p></li><li><p>Fetches the policy row for its<code>APP_ENV</code></p></li><li><p>Compares:</p><ul><li><p>belowrequired→ hard block</p></li><li><p>belowrecommended, before deadline → soft prompt (+ countdown when 3/2/1 days left)</p></li><li><p>belowrecommended, after deadline → hard block</p></li><li><p>on recommended or newer → no modal</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Update opens the store</p></li><li><p>App writes the driver’s version onto their<code>Drivers</code>row when it changes</p></li></ol><p>Countdown: one shared <code>soft_deadline</code> for everyone (not a personal timer). Example: deadline Thursday → Mon “3 days”, Tue “2”, Wed “1", Thu+ locked until they update.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-21 13:25:06.443+00', '2026-07-23 15:38:10.771992+00', NULL),
	('0212fb4c-9e52-4c64-a3a0-e0301ffe90de', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Driver App - Prompt All Drivers with Missing photos to resubmit', '<p>We lost photos of drivers licenses, medical cards, and insurance photos. if these photos were lost the driver will need to resubmit them. make sure the application will be updated appropriately if the photo was lost and prompt the driver to reupload these photos after the bug is fixed.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-22 13:33:28.515+00', '2026-07-23 15:38:35.389398+00', NULL),
	('1e073015-17ab-401b-9631-15cf06eb7153', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Quotes Cannot show stale data', '<p>• ⁃ Make sure that if a quote is updated a customer cannot see stale data</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:11:25.81+00', NULL, NULL),
	('e350f93d-e347-4ce0-ac09-21357cb8c71d', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Remove Signature what event info changes', '<ul><li><p>When a quote changes, it will force the client to sign the quote again and it will display to the client what changed.</p></li></ul><p>• ⁃ Should also change status back to signed.</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:12:03.778+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b88db001-5245-4ee8-8dc3-4a912e400186', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Upload Signed PDF', '<p>When a customer signs create a signed version of the pdf and upload to the files. (Only works locally???!?!?!?!?!?!?)</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:21:28+00', NULL, NULL),
	('b590beed-1b09-4766-9607-58853eb3dbdb', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'quote screen mobile responsive', '<p>• ⁃ Make sure the quote screen is mobile responsive</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:12:36.561+00', NULL, '2026-07-23 19:21:50.034+00'),
	('b3ec2eb7-3895-497f-8739-5b74dc966c42', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Medical Card Not Showing Up For Max', '<p>Medical card is not showing up when address is in USA. I think it''s a language issue i think Max''s address says США and it''s looking for USA.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 13:15:20.964+00', '2026-07-23 20:31:03.166559+00', NULL),
	('e81b6165-4d16-4b2d-9b20-e6a30fd456ba', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Get Max a new Build for Mobile app', '<p> and see if we''re approved for the apple organization account</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-10 11:30:05.265+00', NULL, '2026-08-10 11:30:16.551+00'),
	('8dd7a992-c519-473e-88be-f6b72d23b74c', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Setup Another meeting with abby to review the sending quotes feature', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-06 13:55:10.476+00', '2026-08-10 16:16:21.058975+00', NULL),
	('05c99728-948c-4fc3-9b87-a1a15ef0e304', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Create Plan for Driver App Improvements', '<p>consolidate all the tasks for the driver app into a SOW document.</p><ul><li><p>Driver Satisfaction Score</p></li><li><p>Drivers Create Backlog Tickets</p></li><li><p>etc.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-10 16:31:31.458+00', NULL, NULL),
	('e41df91b-7fba-41f0-a8d7-874adf9368dc', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Create nice Payment success page', '<p>When a customer pays, create a nice page that just says thank you for your payment. A receipt will be emailed to you shortly. And the only option is to return the the quote page.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-12 18:52:27.137+00', '2026-08-12 19:11:59.147501+00', NULL),
	('9ede7b3f-5950-48a2-928b-919187ddd466', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Does Account Manager and Client get confirmation emails after payment?', '<p>yes. Just checked in production the problem was from the webhook issue</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-12 18:54:17.105+00', '2026-08-12 19:28:37.971671+00', NULL),
	('60d28a01-859f-49c8-8ac4-b6df81b237d0', NULL, NULL, 'Damage Fixed Report', '<p>On the damage report, instead of just reporting major or minor for damages, having a similar toggle that the driver can use to report when something has been fixed- a repaired tab. So if lights weren''t working, and they fixed it on the spot, they would still report it, but mark it as fixed, and it would not add the red or yellow lines to the schedule. Having the ability to upload a photo of the damage/repair they did and the receipt for any parts purchased would be great also. -Thanks Michelle</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '04d8fe31-ba63-4037-8f89-c6383bdcfade', '2026-08-10 17:21:33.897+00', NULL, NULL),
	('759e774a-fa40-43fe-b2b9-9b9d4c7de3a2', '71d6e0b4-ffaa-42c5-9e58-5928044b24e3', NULL, 'A driver can create an account with (passwordless auth)', '<p>when a driver does a passwordless auth the mobile app is not set up to work with this.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-14 13:27:40.067+00', NULL, NULL),
	('f62b637a-677c-4b20-9fc6-ac057de16db8', '438f4c13-7bbf-4dbf-bc85-ee6f86d02bbb', NULL, 'Automated Emails', '<ul><li><p>notify assigned account manager when quote is signed. Acceptance criteria, when customer signs a quote, send an email to the assigned AM. include the customer name, event details, and a direct link back to the event or quote.</p></li><li><p>notify assigned account manager when quote is paid. When customer completes payment, send another email, include the customer name, event details, and a direct link back to the event or quote.</p></li><li><p>If the user does not sign, reminder 2 days before expiry (Between 9-5 eastern time)</p></li><li><p>If they DO sign, then reminder if payment is due once a week.</p></li><li><p>Payment due today email</p></li><li><p>Send thank you email after quote signature, configurable document attachments per sales office, weekly payment reminders, reminder on quote expiry (two days before, business hours only), document expiration reminders for admins. And rather than hard-coding country logic, let each sales office define its own documents (like W-2 or COI, or other forms), so an admin can manage them directly without code changes. And small note, double-check the exact forms you''re sending, because W-2 might need confirming.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-23 19:21:04.216+00', NULL, NULL),
	('cafabf95-121a-49aa-bf7a-1b7062550784', NULL, NULL, 'Should Receipt Reimbursement Submissions Affect Damage Reports?', '<p>If a driver uploads a receipt for a new tire for example then it could notify Maintenance Person for the change that was made to this bleacher and maybe they could close the damage report.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-27 15:06:04.372+00', NULL, NULL),
	('2e65f6b2-da6f-4b4c-9f52-8a928be928f2', NULL, NULL, 'Swap Bleachers Also Swap WorkTrackers?', '<p>Should the swap button include work trackers?</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:32:55.78+00', NULL, NULL),
	('8c4afd12-a852-4d47-b951-1d1c53127adf', NULL, NULL, 'Should the swap button have a date range?', '<p>Should the swap button include a date range?</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:33:23.376+00', NULL, NULL),
	('969d3445-a8c0-4c44-895a-9c3e5c1b08a7', NULL, NULL, 'Account Managers Need to be able to Create and Assign Storage Locations', '<p>Like in the configuration and assets page</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:46:20.761+00', NULL, NULL),
	('db1e8c88-0a44-4cf8-863f-da035086f2c1', NULL, NULL, 'Does Swapping Bleachers Create Alerts Properly?', '<p></p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:56:52.766+00', NULL, NULL),
	('35cbca2f-904c-4bb7-a388-d5a094238459', NULL, NULL, 'Are Alerts Being Displayed for Everyone?', '<p>I had to make a quick fix with powersync rules and they might not be showing for some Account Managers</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:57:25.616+00', NULL, NULL),
	('f6a6a519-a407-4ba7-b72f-d4e3fd75c645', NULL, NULL, 'clickin on event on the dahsboard', '<p>All bleachers reserved for events do not show up when you click on the evernt,  the zone sorting overrides the event sorting,   it should be opposite.   we want to see all the bleacher booked regardless of zones selectex</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', '2026-07-23 19:50:21.415+00', NULL, '2026-07-29 18:05:27.716+00'),
	('070f685d-d28d-4995-a42e-169ce716b464', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Dashboard Red and Yellow Squiggly Lines', '<p>The dashboard should show red squiggles if there is at least one major issue. If there is at least one minor issue and no major then only yellow squiggles. else. Don''t show any squiggles.<br><br><strong>Problem</strong><br>Maintenance is marking these damage reports as resolved but they aren''t always creating maintenance events on the dashboard so resolved damage reports are still being shown on the dashboard.<br><br><br><strong>Solution</strong></p><p>Instead of just marking a damage report as ''Resolved'' make them create a maintenance event to get rid of the damage report on the Damage Reports Page.</p>', 'completed', 0, true, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-29 18:01:36.939+00', '2026-07-30 19:13:31.652494+00', NULL),
	('f9e1f8c8-f1cd-4fb7-9dad-c3754a32970e', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'BR110', '<p>110 Does not let me update the gpt tracker or the home base</p>', 'completed', 0, true, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', '2026-07-28 22:57:11.343+00', '2026-07-29 21:40:49.285492+00', NULL),
	('fce40110-d5f0-4376-9ecb-6f0f3bd928f1', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Drag Drop for Released Work Trackers', '<p>make sure there''s like a warning or something? And whenever a work tracker changes, switch back to released and not accepted.</p><p>Edge Cases:</p><ul><li><p>If the worktracker is in progress, probably don''t change anything? Maybe throw a warning to the account manager?</p></li><li><p>When dragging and dropping a accepted work tracker do the same thing. Should probably also display a popup if you think its not too annoying.</p></li><li><p>Make sure to abide by exisitng junior account manager permissions.</p><ul><li><p>(They cannot release them and so they cannot edit work trackers that are released and cannot edit even draft work trackers if they weren''t created by themselves.)</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Make sure notification triggers on drag and drop of released work trackers.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'completed', 0, true, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-06-11 12:59:47.073+00', '2026-07-29 21:40:54.402343+00', NULL),
	('221bb526-43c9-4055-8d78-6f5d8e50fa3f', NULL, NULL, 'Should Junior Account managers be able to swap bleachers?', '<p>Denver almost wants todd to swap events not sure. i think they can''t change events they didn''t create.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-06 14:07:23.084+00', NULL, NULL),
	('4f130e61-8170-4f72-90fe-4913fa712f2f', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Complete Next Steps With Apple', '<p>Had to submit information to continue enrolment to organization account so max can make his own provisioning profiles.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-10 11:46:03.193+00', '2026-08-10 11:46:03.424909+00', NULL),
	('e731fb2f-8099-438d-80d2-0e532669ff00', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Create Plan for Maintenance and Quality Assurance', '<p>There are a few tasks regarding the Maintenance and Damage Reporting stuff that we should look at and make an SOW document.</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-10 16:33:10.924+00', NULL, NULL),
	('d3706d25-d6e4-4af0-902e-ad4b692ffc8c', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Create Demonstration of Current Application Usage and How much we can grow', '<ul><li><p>Create a graph that shows current availability. Put together a little summary showing that capacity is not an issue.</p></li><li><p>Backups in a separate location from the standard backups maybe in Google Drive</p></li><li><p>Maybe we don’t need to backup deleted data.</p></li><li><p>Should probably get some numbers on the amount of storage we’re already using etc.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-06 13:43:01.141+00', '2026-08-12 19:28:52.108758+00', NULL),
	('e82aff2d-49ca-43d0-a68b-b557c1dac73b', NULL, NULL, 'deleting worktrackers that have passed that are incorrect', '<p>Aug 6, bleacher 41, debra james was assigned a load, it had to be changed last minute and then the date passed so it marked it as complete not i can''t edit or dete it.</p>', 'completed', 0, true, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '6b080032-c889-4ce5-86e0-5a564a4d97f7', '2026-08-12 17:37:33.67+00', '2026-08-24 16:18:49.612492+00', NULL),
	('223890a7-a2da-4bbe-bd93-d4b1e5ddbb9f', NULL, NULL, 'Work Trackers should Pull Contact', '<p>Work tracker should have nullable FK for picup contact and drop off contact. should be overridable to any text field if you want.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-28 14:53:08.247+00', NULL, '2026-08-24 22:19:40.17+00'),
	('4b641c23-2080-48e3-8ab5-e6cb5e60959a', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Found tax bug. Only works for Admins.', '<p>when creating an event/quote<br>Make sure that you can see tax and discounts in pdfs and quote signing page.</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-03 14:51:08.626+00', '2026-08-03 18:35:11.668656+00', NULL),
	('1dbe5604-0532-4fe1-922e-59509a3593e4', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Allow Account Managers to Assign Drivers to Zones', '<p>Drivers currently need to be added to an Account Manager’s zone before they appear in places such as the Work Tracker driver dropdown. This is not intuitive because the assignment must be completed from the Account Manager’s profile instead of the Driver Profile.</p><p></p><p>Update the Driver Profile so a driver can be assigned to one or more zones directly when the driver is created or edited instead of assigning to an account manager. This should be a multi-select for zones this driver is assigned to.<br><br>Also fix the current Supabase RLS/RBAC permissions error that prevents Account Managers from assigning drivers to their zones. Account Managers should be allowed to manage driver assignments for zones they have access to.</p><p></p><p><strong>Reference:</strong><br>Loom video: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.loom.com/share/0a8db083ec3e4652b803fb5403a0a274">https://www.loom.com/share/0a8db083ec3e4652b803fb5403a0a274</a></p><p></p><p><strong>Acceptance Criteria:</strong></p><ul><li><p>A driver can be assigned to one or more zones from the Driver Profile.</p></li><li><p>Account Managers can add or remove drivers from zones they have permission to manage.</p></li><li><p>Drivers assigned to a zone appear in the appropriate Work Tracker dropdown.</p></li><li><p>Account Managers no longer receive a Supabase permissions error when updating these assignments.</p></li></ul><p></p>', 'completed', 0, true, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-30 14:13:01.4+00', '2026-07-31 13:08:31.21446+00', NULL),
	('5a51287a-7679-4354-837e-3e4d621cd015', NULL, NULL, 'Driver App - Are Thumbnails working properly?', '<p>When uploading photos. create thumbnails. Not super necesarry just a little bit faster loading photos.</p>', 'to_do', 0, true, NULL, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-31 16:18:35.572+00', NULL, NULL),
	('550e24ad-0f1a-4fae-9d71-27c03a618c74', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Make sure the quote screen is mobile responsive & Wording Changes', '<p>We should say other payment methods underneath the pay online button</p><ul><li><p>Alternatively you can pay by ACH or Check. View the confirmation email for details.</p></li></ul><p>Change Overdue to just due. Overdue seems harsh. Red is ok just overdue is bad.<br><br>video: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.loom.com/share/a98ea6cdf66d478090671d58dbfaa500">https://www.loom.com/share/a98ea6cdf66d478090671d58dbfaa500</a></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-07-30 19:22:33.436+00', '2026-07-31 18:04:40.994981+00', NULL),
	('f7cf85a4-d1eb-4f4d-860a-bfa21352c904', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Review and Commit Changes from Max in Powersync repo', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 15:21:23.746+00', '2026-08-06 13:34:34.720489+00', NULL),
	('698834e4-fbb1-4fb6-8c50-b79562502c98', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'When a quote changes, it will force the client to sign', '<p>Should notify the account manager that their changes should notify the client to resign.<br>Don''t notify if bleacher assignments change on dashboard. Should probably notify the client if Line items change meaning 10rows to 15rows for example.</p><p>When a quote changes, it will force the client to sign the quote again and it will display to the client what changed.</p><ul><li><p>Should also change status back to quoted.</p></li></ul><p>• ⁃ If any dates or prices change they need to resign. But if you make changes to notes or contacts they don’t need to resign.</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-03 15:07:31.3+00', NULL, NULL),
	('be8b5470-8328-4ecd-a40b-1b549a625f22', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Stale Data Sign Quote Page', '<p>Come up with best solution for client never signing a quote with stale data.<br><br>Should also probably have a check to see if the data has updated as soon as the client clicks "Sign Quote" it should verify that nothing changed and if it did, then notify the client instead of signing.<br><br></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-03 15:03:10.901+00', '2026-08-05 20:19:37.633707+00', NULL),
	('64a52807-fe15-47cf-8e28-3c08b8f1f94a', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Get Feedback from Justin about the Driver App', '<p>Notes from call</p><ul><li><p>Justin still doesn’t like the current solution for selecting other bleachers because his inspections are being done on the wrong bleacher.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Damage Reports - We need to allow the driver to see the open damage reports for each bleacher they are picking up. Show Date and name stamps for who and when it was reported. And then add text saying not to create duplicate damage reports if the damage that they found has already been reported. Make sure that the drivers don’t think that not submitting a damage report means it’s fixed.</p></li><li><p>Once per week ish when you open the app you need to re-log in. Fix this. Bad if they need to log in while offline.</p></li><li><p>Justin doesn’t really remember seeing the indicator on the actual photo, because it was 3am.</p></li><li><p>Justin still wants a clickable phone number</p></li><li><p>Should maybe add a report a ticket</p></li><li><p>Likes how it looks in dark mode.</p></li><li><p></p></li></ul><p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 16:39:09.567+00', '2026-08-04 16:39:09.925481+00', NULL),
	('579a8b9e-6597-4ddc-80dd-942ce29c1587', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Organize Sprints and Timings in App', '<p></p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 15:21:01.412+00', '2026-08-04 17:28:06.595549+00', NULL),
	('68018894-b95d-4870-b8c2-f772f6353333', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Review Max''s Plan for Stale Data Task', '<p>Max will get me a plan to not allow customers to sign for stale data. Make sure it''s secure and doesn''t expose our data to vulnerabilities.<br><br>Max&nbsp;&nbsp;[1:06 PM]<br></p><p>Hello<br>So here is my plan<br>For PaymentHistory:<br></p><ol><li><p>enable RLS; allow SELECT for staff roles (admin / account manager / viewer) only; deny all INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE for anon and authenticated clients so the table cannot be read or written via PostgREST.</p></li></ol><p>but if we need to be able insert manually clients payments like check/ACH then we need insert/update<br><br>2. stripe already writes history, so there is nothing to change<br><br>For URL just change change <code>/quote/[invoiceNumber]</code> to <code>/quote/[eventUUID]</code><br>so update checkout success/cancel URLs and in-app public links and no redirects from old invoice-number URLs(if we never send them to clients yet)<br><br>For Staleness Detection:</p><ol><li><p>The page is server-rendered, anonymous.</p></li></ol><p>2. We compute acontent hash(deterministic SHA-256 of the client-visible quote fields).<br>3. The browser holds the hash it loaded with, and every 10s calls <code>GET /api/quotes/{id}/version</code>;<br>&nbsp;the server returns the current hash. Client compares the two strings — mismatch → modal.<br>4. The comparison is client-side; the hash is always produced server-side. So it’s mean it load server<br>And because hash load server we need to chose betwern two ways<br>Way number 1:<br>Add <code>content_hash</code> / <code>contract_hash</code> columns to <code>Events</code>, kept up to date by Postgres triggers (pgcrypto) on the event and its related tables. The 10s endpoint reads one indexed column.<br>It’s mean when we updated something in quote we automatically change hash in columns and client page will read it by api<br><br>Way number 2:<br>No columns, no triggers. The 10s endpoint re-runs the existing <code>buildQuoteDocumentData()</code> and hashes it in Node on each request.<br>So it’s mean we recalculating everything on server each 10 sec, it’s not a lot, if it’s not a lot opened quotes, but more opened quotes by clients more server loading, for now it would not be a problem, but it depends on quantity of clients<br><br>Because a quote page has very low concurrency, so the extra query cost is negligible, and 2 removes the entire migration/trigger/type-regen surface. It also gives correct results for shared-entity edits for free, which way 1 only achieves by adding fan-out triggers. Way 1 is worth revisiting only if we ever expect high concurrent viewership of a single quote<br><br>Something like this<br>what do you think?</p><p>[1:06 PM]</p><p>man it took a while to come up with plan)</p><p>Josh Redgrift&nbsp;&nbsp;[1:45 PM]<br></p><p>I like Way number 1 better and I would like you to stop polling when the tab is hidden or inactive if possible. Browsers should allow this functionality but make sure you test on popular browsers as well. I like your idea of using SSR to improve security on the page. Also make sure when client signs the quote it checks for changes before submitting the signing.</p><p>[1:45 PM]</p><p>Thanks a lot Max)</p><p>[1:47 PM]</p><p>Could you make sure you have the architecture written out in detail for this feature in a markdown file in the repo? I think this is necessary to document</p><p>Max&nbsp;&nbsp;[1:48 PM]<br></p><p>Yes, sure</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 15:23:38.166+00', '2026-08-04 17:48:18.372496+00', NULL),
	('e398a9cb-6f73-4aa0-a418-d7e0018cdd07', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Fix Who Sent the Quote', '<p>Will the quote come from the person who clicked "Send Quote" Or the assigned account manager?</p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '43f82f56-f6e2-4400-aeb2-7c5195c557ad', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-06 13:16:48.379+00', NULL, NULL),
	('e396ac04-eae5-44c7-92cd-7b271cd9198d', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Review a Changes to Bug Fixes in Web App Repo', '<p>Found some bugs for max to fix before deployment</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 15:21:47.279+00', '2026-08-06 13:35:46.76832+00', NULL),
	('6ef204a0-3d85-476c-a2da-ff41e34bdcf0', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Figure out why Server Needs to be restarted once a week', '<p>I made some changes to powersync that might affect the routing so i will wait and see how it goes from here. if the server goes down again I will revisit</p>', 'completed', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-04 18:48:34.521+00', '2026-08-06 13:37:20.452007+00', NULL),
	('214a5aa3-ae6d-4516-841a-a105f9b85956', '971bd9a8-2a95-44b8-b870-b862309e8417', NULL, 'Add Abbys Changes to Email Templates', '<p></p>', 'to_do', 0, false, '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '9bddb34c-d84e-4d11-852a-27f16de08379', '2026-08-06 13:42:32.023+00', NULL, NULL),
